                },
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/logs_and_services_menu/test_event_logs_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 169,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "Verify Valid Content Search Logs (capitalise \"Valid\")"
                },
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/logs_and_services_menu/test_event_logs_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 169,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "```\nVerify valid Content Search Logs\n    [Documentation]  Input valid PEL ID in the search log and verify the results.\n    [Tags]  Verify_Valid_Content_Search_Logs\n    [Setup]  Run Keywords  Redfish.Login  AND  Redfish Purge Event Log\n    [Teardown]  Redfish.Logout\n```\nConsistent with Verify Resolving Single Error Log In GUI and other tests in this suite that create and verify event log state \u2014 each test should start from a known clean state. Without isolation, the test cannot reliably fail when the search feature is broken if residual logs happen to match the query."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/logs_and_services_menu/test_event_logs_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 169,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nandakumar B",
                        "email": "nandakumarb@ami.com",
                        "username": "Nandakumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi George, have added \"Redfish Purge Event Log\" keyword in setup.\nBut for Redfish.Login and Redfish.Logout it is already added in Suite Setup Execution and Suite Teardown Execution.\nEven after execution of \"Redfish Purge Event Log\", A single clear log will be generated, so we need to delete that particular log as well. Hence added new lines to delete it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/logs_and_services_menu/test_event_logs_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 169,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nandakumar B",
                        "email": "nandakumarb@ami.com",
                        "username": "Nandakumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/logs_and_services_menu/test_event_logs_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 222,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "```\n[Setup]     Run Keywords  Redfish.Login  AND  Redfish Purge Event Log\n[Teardown]  Redfish.Logout\n```\n\nConsistent session lifecycle management prevents test interference and follows the established pattern across the entire suite."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/logs_and_services_menu/test_event_logs_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 222,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nandakumar B",
                        "email": "nandakumarb@ami.com",
                        "username": "Nandakumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "Updated the test case, removed the Redfish.Login"
                },
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/logs_and_services_menu/test_event_logs_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 232,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "```\nClick Element  ${xpath_event_logs_resolve}   <--- after this line , add the bellow\n\nWait Until Page Contains  Successfully resolved ${number_of_events} logs.  timeout=10\n```\n\nThe test could pass for the wrong count if Redfish has already updated by the time Get Number Of Event Logs is called post-resolve."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/logs_and_services_menu/test_event_logs_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 232,
                    "reviewer": {
